course: dictionary
lesson: 583
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «They asked for an autograph.» Here an autograph is a famous person's signature, the name they write for a fan to keep. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A signature fits, but a fish or a bus does not.
explain: The same word can also be a verb, a doing word. «Can you autograph my book?» Now autograph means to sign your name on something. Look at the words around it to see which job it does: a or an before it usually means a noun, and a word like can, will or to before it usually means a verb.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «They asked for a signature» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. If your meaning does not fit, like «They asked for a fish», go back and look at the clues again.
fact: An autograph is a famous person's signature, written for a fan to keep.
fact: To autograph something means to sign your name on it, such as a book, photo or shirt.
fact: An autograph book is where friends sign their names, often at the end of a school year.
fact: Formally, an autograph can also be a piece of writing in the author's own hand.
fact: Autograph comes from two Greek parts: auto means self, and graph means writing.
exercise: «They asked for an autograph.» What does autograph mean here? | A kind of cake | A loud shout across the playground | *A famous person's signature, written for a fan to keep | A map of the town
exercise: In «Please autograph my shirt», what job does autograph do? | *To sign your name on something | A kind of shirt | A famous singer | To wash the shirt
exercise: Which meaning of autograph is the formal one? | *A piece of writing in the author's own hand | A famous singer's song | A pen that writes in gold | A school bell
test: Ella's friends sign her autograph book at the end of term. What is an autograph book? | A book of maps | *A book where friends sign their names | A book about famous people's houses | A book for playing games
test: «Will you autograph this photo for me?» In this sentence, autograph is a | *A verb, a doing word | A noun, a thing you can hold | An adjective, a describing word | A number
exam: Read «The star was happy to autograph shirts for her fans.» What does autograph mean here? | To sell shirts at the market | *To sign her name on the shirts for her fans | To wash the shirts | To count the fans
